@startuml "Composite - File System - Class Diagram"
skinparam linetype polyline
skinparam nodesep 90
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor<<spacer>> transparent
  BorderColor<<spacer>> transparent
  FontColor<<spacer>> transparent
}
hide <<spacer>> stereotype
hide <<spacer>> circle
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members
title Composite — a file system, and six questions answered at any depth
skinparam ranksep 16
interface Storage <<Component>> {
  .. roll-ups ..
  + size() : long
  + count() : int
  + lastModified() : Instant
  + largest() : Optional<Storage>
  + find(name) : Optional<Storage>
  + findAll(test) : List<Storage>
  + render(indent) : String
  .. element operations ..
  + rename(name)
  + save()
  + delete()
  + copy() : Storage
  + move(target)
}

interface StorageContainer {
  + add(element)
  + remove(element)
  + elements() : List<Storage>
  + iterator() : StorageIterator
}

abstract class StorageElement {
  - name : String
  - parent : Directory
  - modified : Instant
}

class File <<Leaf>> {
  - bytes : long
}

abstract class Link <<Leaf>> {
  - target : Storage
}

class Directory <<Composite>> {
  - elements : List<Storage>
  - cachedSize : long
  ~ invalidate()
}

class DiskReport <<Client>> {
  - root : Storage
  + totalBytes() : long
  + biggest() : String
}

Storage <|.. StorageElement
StorageElement <|-- File
StorageElement <|-- Link
class " " as Spacer1 <<spacer>>
StorageElement -[hidden]- Spacer1
StorageElement <|-- Directory
StorageContainer <|.. Directory

note bottom of Directory
  Every operation is the same two lines:
  do this directory's part, then ask
  the children to do theirs.
end note

note top of DiskReport
  Names <b>Storage</b> and nothing else.
  Hand it one file and every
  answer is still right.
end note

note bottom of Storage
  <b>Roll-ups</b> aggregate; <b>element operations</b>
  do not. A Component interface grows —
  GoF list "overly general" as a liability.
end note

note right of Link
  A link is its own 64 bytes, <b>not</b> the
  size of its target, or size() on a
  root would double-count.
end note

note bottom of File
  <b>cachedSize</b> + <b>invalidate()</b> are GoF
  implementation issue 8. A change
  invalidates its ancestors <b>upward</b> —
  which is what the parent reference is for.
end note

Directory o-[norank]-> "*" Storage
Directory -[norank]-> Directory : "parent"
DiskReport -[norank]-> Storage
@enduml
